&lt;p&gt;Our high-touch customers are where the relationship, the stakes, and the revenue are biggest. This role makes sure that book is run like a business: clear on who we serve and how, deliberate about the experience we create, and measured on what it delivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is half strategy, half operator. You&#39;ll design customer experiences and programs for our highest-value accounts, and you&#39;ll build the operating rhythm, metrics, and processes that keep the high-touch team effective as it grows. You&#39;ll work directly with CS leadership, CSMs, Sales, Support, Product, and Marketing, and you&#39;ll have room to shape how we serve our biggest customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the high-touch customer experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and pilot the moments that matter for high-touch customers: onboarding to value, executive engagement, business reviews, renewal and expansion plays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what high-touch should mean: which customers qualify, what they get, and what outcome each touchpoint should create.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn customer feedback and data into specific changes to programs, playbooks, and engagement models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Support, Marketing, and Sales to close gaps that customers feel across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the high-touch business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operating model for the high-touch segment: coverage, capacity, cost to serve, and how the model changes as the customer base grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the metrics that tell us whether it&#39;s working, such as adoption, retention, expansion, and customer sentiment, and build the cadence to review them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the planning cycles for the segment, and make the case for where to invest and where to automate or pool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbooks, workflows, and tooling the team uses, and keep them current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead projects across teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a portfolio of strategic and operational projects from ambiguous idea to launched, measured program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate leadership priorities into plans with clear owners, timelines, and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure to cross-functional problems, flag risks early, and drive adoption of new ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear, decision-ready materials for leadership, with a recommendation attached.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years in Customer Success, CS Operations, strategy, or program management, ideally in SaaS, with time close to enterprise or high-touch customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve designed a customer program or operating model and can show what changed because of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in outcomes first. You can say what problem you&#39;re solving, how you&#39;ll know it worked, and what you&#39;d stop doing to make room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with data. You can build the analysis yourself in tools like Salesforce, Gainsight, Tableau, or Snowflake, or ask sharp questions of someone who can.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You influence without authority, and people across Sales, Support, Product, and CS want you in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write and present clearly, and you can lead with the answer for executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You like building new things and also making them stick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI or automation to scale customer engagement and CSM efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer segmentation, health scoring, or customer journey design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program or project management certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
