&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Product Data Scientist, Forecasting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Klaviyo&#39;s Product Data Science team plays a critical role in shaping how we understand, measure, and improve business performance. We partner closely with Product, Engineering, Finance, and Go-to-Market teams to turn complex data into actionable insights that inform product strategy, financial planning, and long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Klaviyo continues to scale its platform, expand its product portfolio, and introduce new AI-powered capabilities, the ability to accurately forecast business outcomes and understand the drivers behind them has never been more important.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team combines rigorous statistical modeling, advanced analytics, and deep business understanding to help leaders make better decisions. We believe data science should be embedded in the product development lifecycle, influencing strategic investments, identifying opportunities, and enabling teams to move quickly and confidently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Lead Product Data Scientist, Forecasting to own and advance Klaviyo&#39;s forecasting capabilities, combining deep technical expertise with strong business judgment to influence some of our most important product and strategic decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, hands-on technical leadership role at the intersection of data science, product strategy, and business performance. You&#39;ll lead the development of sophisticated revenue forecasting models, establish rigorous evaluation standards, and help the organization better understand how customer behavior, product investments, pricing decisions, and market dynamics influence business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t just about building accurate models or reporting on historical trends. We&#39;re looking for someone who can connect advanced statistical methods to real business questions, challenge assumptions, investigate unexpected outcomes, and translate complex findings into clear recommendations that shape decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product, Finance, Engineering, and Go-to-Market leadership to build scalable forecasting systems and self-service analytical capabilities. You&#39;ll also help define the technical direction of forecasting at Klaviyo, mentor other data scientists, and establish the methodologies and standards that make forecasting a trusted, repeatable practice across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make a Difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own revenue forecasting end to end&lt;/strong&gt;, from problem framing and data preparation through model development, evaluation, deployment, and ongoing monitoring, ensuring forecasts serve as trusted inputs to business planning and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build sophisticated forecasting models&lt;/strong&gt; across multiple time horizons and levels of granularity, leveraging hierarchical forecasting, probabilistic and Bayesian methods, classical time series techniques, machine learning, and emerging time series foundation models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish forecasting standards and governance&lt;/strong&gt; by defining how the organization measures accuracy, bias, calibration, and uncertainty, creating consistent and rigorous approaches to model evaluation and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the technical direction of forecasting&lt;/strong&gt;, evaluating modeling approaches, reviewing technical designs, mentoring other data scientists, and raising the bar for statistical methodology, code quality, and analytical rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect forecasting to business strategy&lt;/strong&gt; by partnering with Product, Finance, Engineering, and Go-to-Market teams to support scenario planning, evaluate strategic investments, and translate ambiguous business questions into actionable analytical plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Uncover drivers of customer and product performance&lt;/strong&gt; through advanced statistical research, including mixed effects models, clustering, time series analysis, and other techniques that reveal meaningful patterns and inform product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead root cause investigations&lt;/strong&gt; when actual business performance diverges from forecasts, identifying whether changes stem from data quality, model limitations, customer behavior, product or pricing decisions, or external factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable root cause analysis frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; through repeatable methodologies, templates, and dashboards, enabling other data scientists and business stakeholders to investigate performance consistently and efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop self-service forecasting and analytics capabilities&lt;/strong&gt; that empower product managers and cross-functional leaders to explore business trends, evaluate scenarios, and make informed decisions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Data Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to build reliable data pipelines and dbt models that provide clean, well-structured, and trustworthy data for forecasting and downstream analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate emerging AI and forecasting technologies&lt;/strong&gt;, identifying opportunities to leverage new modeling techniques, time series foundation models, and AI-powered tools to improve accuracy, efficiency, and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence decisions across the organization&lt;/strong&gt; by communicating complex statistical findings and business implications clearly and persuasively to stakeholders ranging from individual contributors to executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 10+ years of experience in data science, product analytics, applied statistics, or a related quantitative discipline, including significant hands-on experience building and deploying forecasting solutions in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring deep expertise in time series forecasting, statistical modeling, and model evaluation, with experience applying methods such as hierarchical forecasting, probabilistic or Bayesian approaches, and machine learning to complex business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re highly proficient in SQL and Python or R, with experience developing production-quality analytical solutions and familiarity with dbt and modern analytics engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve demonstrated technical leadership by setting direction on complex projects, mentoring other data scientists, reviewing modeling approaches, and influencing technical standards across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You combine statistical rigor with strong business intuition and understand how product development, customer behavior, pricing, and strategic investments translate into measurable financial and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable owning complex analytical problems from initial exploration through production deployment, ongoing monitoring, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can translate ambiguous business questions into well-defined analytical approaches, establish meaningful success metrics, and deliver actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a compelling communicator who can explain sophisticated statistical concepts and modeling tradeoffs to both technical and non-technical audiences, including senior executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in cross-functional environments and enjoy partnering with Product, Finance, Engineering, and business leaders to influence strategic decisions and improve customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable operating in ambiguity, move with urgency, and know how to balance analytical rigor with the speed and iteration required in a high-growth product environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring an AI-first mindset, with curiosity and familiarity around emerging technologies such as time series foundation models, LLMs, and agentic tools that can improve forecasting, analytical workflows, and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Economics, Finance, Engineering, or another quantitative discipline, or an MBA with a quantitative emphasis. Equivalent hands-on experience in applied forecasting or statistical modeling is equally valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling forecasting capabilities in a high-growth B2B SaaS or product-focused technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with revenue forecasting, financial modeling, scenario planning, or business performance analysis in a subscription-based business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud data platforms, distributed processing systems, and modern data engineering infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying advanced statistical methods, including mixed effects models, clustering, and probabilistic modeling, to understand customer behavior and product performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building self-service analytics tools, dashboards, or forecasting platforms used by cross-functional business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on exposure to emerging time series foundation models, LLMs, or agentic AI applications for forecasting and decision support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing forecasting governance, model evaluation frameworks, or standardized root cause analysis practices across an organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forecasting is fundamental to how Klaviyo evaluates business performance, makes strategic investments, and plans for the future. As our business and product portfolio become more sophisticated, the ability to understand not just what is happening, but what is likely to happen next and why, is increasingly important.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll help establish forecasting as a core organizational capability, shaping the models, methodologies, and analytical standards that inform critical product and business decisions. Your work will directly influence how leaders evaluate growth opportunities, understand customer behavior, measure the impact of product investments, and respond to changing business conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to combine deep technical ownership with meaningful strategic influence, working alongside a highly collaborative data science team to build scalable capabilities that have a lasting impact on Klaviyo&#39;s growth and decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary range reflects the cost of labor across various U.S. geographic markets. The range displayed below reflects the minimum and maximum target salaries for the position across all our US locations. The base salary offered for this position is determined by several factors, including the applicant’s job-related skills, relevant experience, education or training, and work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, our total compensation package may include participation in the company’s annual cash bonus plan, variable compensation (OTE) for sales and customer success roles, equity, sign-on payments, and a comprehensive range of health, welfare, and wellbeing benefits based on eligibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruiter can provide more details about the specific salary/OTE range for your preferred location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range For US Locations:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$258,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may require up to 10% travel for purposes such as new hire onboarding, client or partner work if applicable, team meetings, and industry events. Travel is coordinated in advance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Klaviyo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Klaviyo (pronounced clay-vee-oh). We empower creators to own their destiny by making first-party data accessible and actionable like never before. We see limitless potential for the technology we’re developing to nurture personalized experiences in ecommerce and beyond. To reach our goals, we need our own crew of remarkable creators—ambitious and collaborative teammates who stay focused on our north star: delighting our customers. If you’re ready to do the best work of your career, where you’ll be welcomed as your whole self from day one and supported with generous benefits, we hope you’ll join us.&lt;/p&gt;
