&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Public Relations Lead who&#39;s always plugged into what&#39;s trending. Someone who knows which brand&#39;s marketing is having a moment, which campaign just went viral, and what CMOs are talking about right now. And already thinking about how to insert Klaviyo into that conversation. You&#39;ll tell that story to brand marketers, CMOs, and the customers we serve. You&#39;ll be responsible for building out our biggest research moments including Black Friday/Cyber Monday and quarterly reports on the trends marketers care about most. This is a role for someone who&#39;s fully entrenched in what good marketing looks like, quick to newsjack a great campaign, and driven to build the story so our customers see the role Klaviyo can play in it too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make a Difference:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the press office day-to-day in partnership with our PR agencies, proactively pitching stories, securing high-impact coverage, and building relationships with reporters and influencers across marketing, retail, and commerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a close pulse on marketing, commerce, and the broader news cycle — know what&#39;s trending, move fast to newsjack the moments worth jumping on, and draft exec statements and comments that can go out same-day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I&lt;/strong&gt;dentify and secure speaker opportunities at key events and award opportunities to amplify Klaviyo’s thought leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive thought leadership programs for our CMO and other key executives, developing compelling points of view and identifying opportunities to build their presence in market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Marketing to find the customers with the most compelling stories for press.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our thought leadership research arm, the stake-in-the-ground research that fuels our storytelling, from shaping our BFCM story each year to planning what research we&#39;ll publish every quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the creative energy to our biggest moments like K:BOS and K:LDN: get press to the event, organize panelists, and build the brand story around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use and build AI tools to automate and speed up the team&#39;s workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine, active interest in marketing and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep relationships with reporters covering marketing, retail, and commerce, and familiarity with emerging channels and influencers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a press office and moving fast — comfortable making the call on what&#39;s newsworthy without waiting for direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing skills, with the ability to turn research and trends into sharp, pitchable narratives and exec talking points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with executives on thought leadership — shaping their point of view and building their presence in market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools to move faster, with a collaborative, self-starter mindset who can run with ideas and execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, Marketing, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience in public relations, communications, media relations, or a related field, including experience in-house and/or at an agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting marketing, retail, ecommerce, technology, or other relevant consumer-facing industries preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience running media relations programs, securing earned media coverage, and developing thought leadership and research-driven communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
